                  <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_422">Oxford,
                        Oxfordshire, Carmelite convent</orgName><p>This attribution was first listed
                        (with a query) in the Medieval Libraries of Great Britain Supplement (1987),
                        with the following footnote: <q>Copied <q>iussu Burelli Oxonii</q> from the
                           MS. now Leyden, Voss. lat. F.33, which was brought <q>ex anglia</q> by
                              <persName>Lawrence Burrell</persName>, provincial of Narbonne, and
                           given by him to the Carmelites of Paris in 1494. The Stockholm MS. may be
                           the copy which Leland saw in Oxford (<title>Collectanea</title>, iv
                           (1774), 59).</q> This footnote paraphrases the details that were
                        originally recorded on the corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain
                        index card (in Neil Ker's handwriting). However, this index card also
                        includes a later note, <q>Rejected 1989; see card in rejected sequence</q>.
                        No such index card was found in the rejected books section during data
                        reconciliation work undertaken in 2026.</p></provenance>
